            "label": "Very High Body Awareness",
            "range": { "min": 72, "max": 90 },
            "color": "#f97316",
            "description": "Very high interoceptive awareness, may indicate hypervigilance to bodily sensations."
        }
    ],

    "interpretation": {
        "scoringMethod": "Sum all item scores (range 18-90). Subscale scores can be calculated separately. Higher scores indicate greater body/interoceptive awareness.",
        "clinicalContext": "The BPQ-SF measures interoception - the sense of the internal state of the body. Altered interoception is associated with anxiety, depression, autism spectrum conditions, and various somatic disorders.",
        "bidirectionalInterpretation": "Both very low and very high scores may be clinically relevant. Low scores may indicate disconnection from bodily signals; high scores may indicate hypervigilance or somatic focus.",
        "populationNorms": "Healthy adults typically score in the moderate range (36-53)."
    },

